<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's bank liquidity up 0.15 pct.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's bank liquidity up 0.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said on Monday that liquidity in the bank system grew 0.15 percent, or 23 million sucres, to 15.02 billion sucres in the week to August 16.</p>
<p>In August 9, bank liquidity reached 14.99 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector ended 1995 at 12.51 billion sucres, up 41.2 percent from 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258-433</p>
</text>
